sections.full_text:
(1) This Act shall apply to—
(a) all securities hereafter created or issued by or on behalf of the Government of the Federation;
(b) securities hereafter created or issued by or on behalf of the Government of a State which are declared by the President by notice in the Federal Gazette to be securities to which this Act applies;
(c) securities declared by the President by notice in the Federal Gazette to be securities to which this Act applies, being securities created or issued by companies or corporations incorporated directly by an Act enacted by the National Assembly or by a Law enacted by the House of Assembly of a State;
(d) debentures and fully paid-up shares of any company incorporated and registered under the Companies and Allied Matters Act (other than a private company).
(2) The power of a trustee to invest in debentures and shares under paragraph (d) of subsection (1) of this section shall be subject to the statutory restrictions and qualifications set forth in the Schedule to this Act.

